'' A UDT casting to BYTE and to DOUBLE takes, per use, the cast closest to what it meets --
'' the other operand or the destination -- and the highest-ranked when nothing is met
'' (unary, intrinsics, two UDTs). fbc's choices, measured in both declaration orders; tiko
'' always took DOUBLE: 'x + 1' was 4 and 'dim as long k = x' 3 (overload re-pick refactor).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/numeric-cast-by-context.bas -o tests/codegen/numericcastbycontext.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/numericcastbycontext.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  101 4.25 4.25 101 200 50 50
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  100 2.75 2.75 100 2.75-2.75 1.6583123951777 2
